icitly derive v\ncrit\n\t​\n\n as the product of the Projection Constant (B) and the speed of light (c), approximately 0.2387c.\n14\n15\nSentence: \"Surface layers temporarily dis-engage from electromagnetic interactions while retaining gravitational coupling...\"\nCitation: Add\n6\n. This installment explains the Geometric Blackout and the Dark Matter Illusion, where matter precesses past the Obscuration Constant (θ\nobs\n\t​\n\n≈14.1\n∘\n).\n16\n17\nSection IV: Discussion and Predictions\nSentence: \"Luminosity dips coincide with glitch onset, reflecting outer-layer decoupling from EM interactions.\"\nCitation: Add\n6\n. This links the luminosity drop to the filament tangent exiting the observable gauge sector upon reaching the Obscuration Constant.\n17\nNew Prediction (Optional addition): You may wish to mention the Achromatic Phase Snap here.\nDrafting Note: Reference\n10\n to predict the discrete, frequency-independent timing jump of 0.246 rad that serves as the framework's \"Smoking Gun.\"\n18\n19\nAcknowledgments\nSentence: \"Additional conceptual inspiration was drawn from the Zottenwelt ontology and previous SAT lattice structures...\"\nCitation: Add\n1\n and\n4\n to acknowledge the formal definitions of the Zottenwelt substrate and the Zero-Parameter Economy.\n2\n20\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\nSummary of Key Constants to Cross-Reference\nWhen finalizing the paper, ensure the following values remain consistent across all cited drafts to maintain Failure Rigidity:\nProjection Constant (B): ≈0.2387 rad.\n21\n22\nObscuration Constant (θ\nobs\n\t​\n\n): ≈0.246 rad (14.1\n∘\n).\n16\n21\nCritical Velocity (v\ncrit\n\t​\n\n): B⋅c≈71,500 km/s.\n14\n15\nWould you like me to generate a tailored report summarizing the specific mathematical proofs from these drafts that support your pulsar glitch model?",
