      "text": "Foundational Ontology (The Zottenwelt)\nZottenwelt (\"Shaggy World\"): A purely Euclidean 4-space (R\n4\n) with a (+,+,+,+) metric signature, re-architecting reality as a dense, physical fabric of one-dimensional filaments\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nEvolving Block Universe (EBU): A dynamic 4D structure where time is the physical expansion of a 3D Time Surface (or Timesheet) propagating at the speed of time (c)\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nIntersectional Trace: The concept that what we perceive as a fundamental particle is the 3D manifestation of a 4D worldline filament piercing the moving timesheet\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nRadial World Manifold: An architecture where the history of a particle is a 4D radial sector rather than a linearized line, with light and matter following distinct expansion regimes\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nThe Mathematical Engine\nMaster SAT Lagrangian (L\nSAT\n\t​\n\n): A scale-invariant action functional governing energy transfer between the 4D network and the 3D wavefront, integrating kinetic, projective, and interaction energies\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nRelativistic-Quantum Isomorphism: The core proof that General Relativity (low-frequency global bending) and Quantum Mechanics (high-frequency discrete vibrations) are isomorphic projections of the same 4D superhelical dynamics\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nFourth-Order Governing Equation: An analytical worldline formalism used to prevent \"curvature spikes\" and singularities, ensuring path differentiability up to the fourth order\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nLaplace-Beltrami Operator: Used on the S\n3\n manifold to derive quantum discreteness and the hydrogen energy ladder from standing-wave harmonics\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nBV Pushforward (P\n∬\n\t​\n\n): A projection engine that integrates out high-frequency 4D coiling histories (Ultraviolet) to produce effective 3D observables (Infrared)\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nStructural Invariants (The Zero-Parameter Economy)\nProjection Constant (B=3/4π≈0.2387 rad): The fundamental per-dimension distortion factor governing 4D-to-3D lattice closure and the critical velocity threshold (v\ncrit\n\t​\n\n≈0.2387c)\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nAchromatic Phase Snap (Φ≈0.246 rad / 14.1°): A mandatory structural invariant/reset required for holonomy closure when worldlines hit the Geometric Corner\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nFilament Scale (ℓ\nf\n\t​\n\n≈0.7937 fm): The fundamental unit of distance, re-architected as the Topological Saturation Limit and pinned to the Rydberg Constant\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nMinimal Curvature Regulator (ϵ≈2×10\n−21\n m): The hard mechanical resolution limit (string thickness) that prevents mathematical singularities and interaction energy divergences\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nDirac CP Phase Lock (270\n∘\n): An inevitability of lattice closure derived from integrating rotational torsion over the S\n3\n manifold\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nParticle Taxonomy & Force Unification\nTopological Charge (Q): A dimensionless invariant (Q=L\nwind\n\t​\n\n+L\nlink\n\t​\n\n+W\nwrithe\n\t​\n\n) used to derive the particle mass hierarchy; stable configurations are capped by the UV Finiteness Lock (Q≤3)\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nBorromean Triplets (Baryons): Stable 3-filament braids where stability requires all three strands, providing a geometric derivation of quark confinement\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nHopf Links (Mesons): Intersectional traces of 2-filament braids\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nTrue Bosons vs. True Fermions: Fermions are persistent 4D coils, while bosons (photons, gravitons) are transient excitations or ripples propagating parasitically through the filament ensemble\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nElectrogravity Unification: A model identifying electromagnetism as high-frequency Toroidal Vortex induction in the time wave and gravity as its low-frequency, charge-cancelled macroscopic limit\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nStrong Force: Re-architected as Braid Rigidity—the geometric resistance of interlocked worldlines to being de-braided\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nKey Phenomena & Resolved Anomalies\nMass as Projective Resistance (R): The mechanical drag/back-push encountered by a 4D world tube resisting the radial expansion of the timesheet\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nGravity as Forward Pull: The cumulative Topological Tension of worldlines being pulled taut against the knots of historical interaction\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nDark Matter Illusion: Matter that has precessed past the Obscuration Constant (≈14.1\n∘\n), losing its 3D gauge coupling (becoming 80% darker) while retaining its gravitational persistence\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nPulsar Glitches: Mandatory Quantized Holonomy Transitions (structural resets) triggered when rotating bodies breach the critical velocity threshold\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nBraid Smoothing: A non-linear mechanism where intensive inter-braiding in dense nuclei paradoxically reduces total resolution resistance\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nNeutrino Precession: A model explaining flavor oscillation as a mechanical residual caused by the worldline corkscrewing through geometric slots in the lattice\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nComputational & Speculative Tools\nTopological Indicatrix (TX) / Universal Indicatrix (UI): A geometric generator/translator that maps 4D worldlines to 3D trajectories using rotation matrices (SO(4)) and radial expansion\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nWhirligig Engine: A computational device mapping logical derivations as physical geometric paths on a unit 3-sphere to identify shortest path derivations between theories\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nThe Donut (Torus): A mapping surface where the interaction of two equations is visualized as a Lissajous Curve, acting as a physical computer for geometric differentiation\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nLattice Navigator: Speculative macroscopic spaceflight mechanics utilizing \"time feathering\" (pitch adjustment) to neutralize projective resistance and navigate the 4D bulk\nlock\nmore_horiz\n.\nComplexity Inversion: A nonlinear transition in superheavy attractors (e.g., Harmonium-620) where high 